Smarty Pants on openSUSE Tumbleweed
=================================

This package includes local CPU inference, DeepSeek and compatible APIs.
Model weights download only when a local rewrite is first requested.

Start Smarty Pants from your application launcher, or run:

    /usr/bin/smarty-pants daemon start

Use a Wayland session with a StatusNotifierItem tray host, such as Waybar
with its tray module enabled. Zenity supplies the settings and review
dialogs. On a fresh installation, local Qwen inference is the default.

For DeepSeek:

1. Open the tray and select Provider -> DeepSeek (cloud).
2. Choose Set API key... and enter the key in the local dialog.
3. Select API model -> DeepSeek V4 Flash, DeepSeek V4 Pro, or Custom model.
4. Choose Rewrite delivery -> Review, then copy... for the first test.

DeepSeek usage is billed by DeepSeek. Selecting it does not download or
load local weights. API keys are stored in a separate private file in
your configuration directory, never in the package or its sources.

Bind a compositor shortcut to:

    /usr/bin/smarty-pants trigger --mode rewrite

Other modes are academic, linkedin and condense. Keep the intended text
selected when triggering a rewrite. Verify meaning and facts in outputs.

Optional login startup
---------------------

Quit a manually launched daemon before starting the user service. From
your graphical session, import WAYLAND_DISPLAY and whichever compositor
variables apply (HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE, SWAYSOCK or NIRI_SOCKET):

    systemctl --user import-environment WAYLAND_DISPLAY
    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    systemctl --user enable --now smarty-pants.service

The unit follows graphical-session.target. Minimal compositor setups may
need to activate that target or use their own startup configuration.

After an RPM upgrade, restart an already running daemon to use the new
binary:

    systemctl --user restart smarty-pants.service

Migrating an existing installation
---------------------------------

Check `systemctl --user cat smarty-pants.service` and
`systemctl --user show smarty-pants.service --property=ExecStart` first.
A unit in ~/.config/systemd/user takes precedence over this package's unit
and may still point at ~/.cargo/bin or ~/.local/bin. Preserve its settings
and drop-ins, update ExecStart to /usr/bin/smarty-pants-daemon, reload the
user manager, and restart when idle. Check shortcut and launcher paths
for the same precedence issue. Do not run two daemons at once.

User configuration and credentials remain under the XDG configuration
directory (normally ~/.config/smarty-pants). Never overwrite them with
the example at /usr/share/smarty-pants/examples/deepseek.toml.

Diagnostics:

    /usr/bin/smarty-pants status
    journalctl --user -u smarty-pants.service

Online instructions: https://github.com/thbertoldi/smarty-pants
